      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1">The framed manuscript page number [ⲓⲅ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke.</p>
        <p n="2">Measured strokes: in the first ϩⲛ̄ the stroke covers ϩ by 50 % and ⲛ by 60 % (encoded on both); in the second it covers ϩ by 43 % and ⲛ by 53 % (encoded on ⲛ only).</p>
        <p n="6">⟨ⲧⲉ⟩ is the editors' correction (apparatus: read ⲟⲩ⟨ⲧⲉ⟩).</p>
        <p n="11">The editors offer [ⲙⲁⲑⲏⲧⲏⲥ] or [ⲁⲡⲟⲥⲧⲟⲗⲟⲥ] (apparatus). The edition prints the opening bracket after ⲛ̄ and no closing bracket; the restoration and the five lost letters after it are taken to run to the end of the line. ⲓⲏⲥ is printed without an overline here.</p>
        <p n="14">Lines 14–15: the editors print, with a brace over both lines, that they are almost completely destroyed; no text is given.</p>
        <p n="15">See l. 14.</p>
        <p n="17">The edition prints a closing bracket after ⲁⲩϫⲉⲥⲧⲟⲩ with no opening bracket.</p>
        <p n="20">The bracket opened before the last eight dots is closed only in l. 21, after ten dots. It is closed here at the line end and reopened in l. 21.</p>
        <p n="21">The bracket before the last four dots is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end.</p>
        <p n="22">The overline of ⲥⲱⲣ (measured) covers ⲥⲱⲣ and not the preceding ⲡ.</p>
        <p n="23">The editors print that the beginning of the line is destroyed and rubbed off; the fifteen dots that follow are their count of illegible letters.</p>
        <p n="24">The edition prints a closing bracket after the nine dots with no opening bracket; the dots are therefore encoded as illegible.</p>
        <p n="30">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ϩ inside the restoration.</p>
        <p n="32">The edition prints a closing bracket after the eight dots with no opening bracket; the dots are therefore encoded as illegible.</p>
      </div>
